<title>USA: UCAR Intl Inc Q4 net income rises.</title>
<headline>UCAR Intl Inc Q4 net income rises.</headline>
<dateline>DANBURY, Conn. 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>3 Mos ended 12/31 Yr ended 12/31</p>
<p>					   1996    1995    1996    1995</p>
<p> Net sales			     $237    $244    $948    $901</p>
<p> Gross profit			    90	99     365     345</p>
<p>Income(loss) before charge,</p>
<p>    effect of acctg change	   37	31     145	25</p>
<p> Extraordinary charge, net of tax  --	19	--	37</p>
<p>Effect of change in accounting</p>
<p>  for inventories			--	--	 7	--</p>
<p>  Net income (loss)		    37	12     152    (12)</p>
<p>Primary net EPS (1995 Pro forma)</p>
<p>  Before items			 0.77    0.65    3.00    1.87</p>
<p>  Acctg change			   --	--    0.15	--</p>
<p>  Primary net EPS		    0.77    0.65    3.15    1.87</p>
<p>Wgtd avg shrs (Pro forma 1995)</p>
<p>    (in thousands)		 48,661  48,922  48,469  48,763</p>
<p>		  (Dollars in millions, except per share data)</p>
<p>NOTE: * Effective January 1, 1996, the Company changed its method of determining LIFO inventories.  The new methodology provides specifically identified parameters for defining new items within the LIFO pool which the Company believes improves the accuracy of costing those items.</p>
<p>The Company recorded income of $7 million (after related taxes of $4 million) as the cumulative effect on prior years of this change in accounting for inventories.</p>
